- Form 1099‑INT — bank/broker interest (Chase, Schwab).
- Schedule A — only if you decide to itemize (to claim the $2,000 charity and any other itemized deductions).
- Schedule B — only if interest/dividend totals exceed the threshold (generally $1,500) or you have certain foreign accounts — your interest total is $1,115, so Schedule B likely not required.
- California state return: CA Form 540 (and associated schedules). State rules differ from federal (including student loan interest and other items) so check CA specifics.

