  - Subtotal = 84,900 + 1,115 + 10,176 = 96,191
  - Half of SE tax (~$719) is an adjustment → estimated AGI ≈ 95,472 before student loan interest deduction
- With AGI in the mid‑$90k range, you may be above the phaseout range and therefore ineligible for the student‑loan interest deduction; if you were below the phaseout you could deduct up to $2,500 (not the full $3,600). Exact phaseout ranges change annually, so I recommend checking the IRS instructions for the tax year or asking a preparer to confirm.
